INT. LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S COTTAGE - KITCHEN - DUSK

A stove, a table, a window full of grey sea. A radio crackles on the shelf.

HANNELORE VOSS (60s, retired keeper, sleeves rolled) peels potatoes. Her daughter INGRID VOSS (30s, city coat still on) hasn't sat down.

Across the table, DESMOND OKAFOR (40s, estate agent, folder in hand) waits with a patient smile.

HANNELORE
Tea?

DESMOND
We're fine, thank you.

HANNELORE
Ingrid?

INGRID
Mum, sit down.

Hannelore keeps peeling. The skin curls into the sink.

DESMOND
The valuation is generous, Mrs. Voss. The Trust will keep the light running.

HANNELORE
It's been running since 1894.

INGRID
It's been failing since 2009.

DESMOND
The structural report was quite specific.

Hannelore sets down the knife. Wipes her hands, slowly, on a cloth.

HANNELORE
She read the report before I did. She always was quick.

Ingrid looks away.

INGRID
Mum.

HANNELORE
Your father painted that railing every spring. She remembers.

The radio hisses.

RADIO (V.O.)
(crackling)
Coastguard to Skerry Light. Weather warning. Gale force nine from the northwest by twenty hundred. Over.

Nobody moves. Hannelore doesn't reach for the handset.

DESMOND
Shouldn't someone answer that?

HANNELORE
It's a recording. They stopped sending real people years ago.

INGRID
Sign it, Mum.

HANNELORE
She wants me gone before the storm.

INGRID
I want you warm.

HANNELORE
I was warm when she left for London.

Ingrid's jaw sets. Desmond slides the folder an inch closer.

HANNELORE (CONT'D)
Don't push that at me.

DESMOND
Mrs. Voss, I only--

INGRID
Just let her breathe.

HANNELORE
Stop talking for me!

DESMOND
It's a standard form!

Both speak at once.

HANNELORE
You sold the house in Kiel.

^INGRID
You buried Dad here.

Silence. The wind finds the window frame.

HANNELORE
He wanted the sea.

INGRID
He wanted you to leave. He told me. In the hospital.

Hannelore hurls the potato. It strikes the wall, bursts, slides down the paint.

HANNELORE
Liar!

Ingrid doesn't flinch. Desmond stands. Nobody sits again.

RADIO (V.O.)
(crackling)
Coastguard to Skerry Light. Do you copy? Over.

Hannelore crosses to the shelf. Picks up the handset. Looks at it. Puts it down.

The pen lies on the folder. She takes it.

FADE OUT.
